--- body ---
## Problem

Housekeeping steps 1/1a/1b (git fetch, gc, beat-skip expiry sweep, erg check) are
fully deterministic but currently run as LLM prose instructions, spending tokens
on work that needs no model judgment. A budget overflow in the ticket-scan phase
(steps 2–6) also taints the git phase's outcome code even when git work committed
cleanly.

## Solution

Extract steps 1, 1a, 1b from `skills/housekeeping/SKILL.md` into
`scripts/housekeeping-git.sh`. Beat.py calls the script as a plain subprocess
(zero token cost) before invoking the skill. The skill's step 1 becomes a single
`Bash(scripts/housekeeping-git.sh)` call for interactive use — no algorithm in
LLM prose.

## Actions

1. Write `scripts/housekeeping-git.sh`:
   - `git fetch --all --prune --quiet && git gc --auto`
   - Beat-skip expiry sweep: remove entries from `.git/beat-skip.json` where
     `until < now` (Python one-liner or jq acceptable)
   - `${ERG:-tickets/erg} check tickets/ 2>/dev/null || true`
   - Exit 0 always (degrade gracefully)

2. Update `skills/housekeeping/SKILL.md`: replace steps 1/1a/1b prose with
   `Bash(scripts/housekeeping-git.sh)`.

3. Update `beat.py` `_housekeeping_phase()`: call the script as a subprocess
   before `run_skill("/housekeeping", ...)`. Log `hk-git:done` or `hk-git:rc=N`
   independently.

## Exit criteria

- `scripts/housekeeping-git.sh` exists, is executable, and passes `bash -n`
- `skills/housekeeping/SKILL.md` steps 1/1a/1b replaced by single Bash call
- `beat.py` logs `hk-git:done` separately from the skill outcome
- `make check` passes
